{"name":"Seraph’s Blush","hex":"#f4d9cb","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seraph","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A burning serpent, often winged, with human hands and sometimes feet; one of God's entourage. On Earth, they strike with burning poison; in Heaven, with burning coal.","A six-winged angel; one of the highest choir or order of angels in Christian angelology, ranked above cherubim, and below God."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seraph"},{"term":"blush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of blushing; a pink or red glow on the face caused by embarrassment, shame, shyness, love, etc.","A glow; a flush of colour, especially pink or red."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become red or pink in the face (and sometimes experience an associated feeling of warmth), especially due to shyness, love, shame, excitement, or embarrassment.","To be shy, ashamed, or embarrassed (to do something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seraph","blocks":[{"text":"A seraph is a celestial or heavenly being originating in Ancient Judaism. The term plays a role in subsequent Judaism, Christianity, and Islam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Bas_Relief%2C_Jerusalem_YMCA_%285503056704%29.jpg/330px-Bas_Relief%2C_Jerusalem_YMCA_%285503056704%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seraph","wikidata":"Q194077"},{"title":"Blush (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush is a medium bright tone of pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blush_rose_1.jpg/330px-Blush_rose_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blush_(color)","wikidata":"Q22133966"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Bas_Relief%2C_Jerusalem_YMCA_%28550305670